  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 149 AM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nA mid level inverted trough of low pressure is forecast to move over \nS TX by Wednesday, which will provide mid/upper level support for \nconvective development, mainly along the daily sea breeze. With the \ndeeper moisture and the weakest capping inversion expected across \nthe Victoria Crossroads, probabilities will be highest up to 60% \nwith lower probabilities south and west. The lowest chance will be \nacross the Rio Grande Plains. Rainfall totals Wednesday through \nFriday are expected to be generally less than 0.5 inch, but with \nPWATs of 2.0-2.3 inches, a few stronger storms may produce 1-2 \ninches. Rain chances are progged to decrease through the weekend as \nmid level ridging builds back across S TX. \n\nWith the ridge comes hotter temperatures and higher heat indices. An \nExtreme risk of heat related impacts are forecast across most of S \nTX by the weekend. Although, heat indices up to 113 may occur \nWednesday and Thursday, it is expected to be isolated with short \nduration, thus Heat Advisories are less likely to be needed. \nHowever, by Friday and into the weekend the duration of heat indices \nof 110+ across a larger area may warrant daily Heat Advisories, \npossibly into early next week.",
